==Strategy==
The best way to tackle this advent is using [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. There's a consistent setup that forces him into Clionel's blind spot:

#Stall out the initial swarm of Relic Doges with [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] until you have enough to afford Bahamut (as well as charge up your Cat Cannon).
#Send him out to instantly clear the field, then send out a [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] instantly.
#Send a [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] as soon as Bahamut triggers the boss wave.
#Bahamut will kill or severely cripple the opening boss wave, letting just one Gabriel through; this Gabriel will instantly rebound Bahamut, causing him to dodge Cruel Angel Clionel's attack (killing the Gabriel in the process).
#Send out a [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] to knock back the Heavenly Hippoe, then use the Cat Cannon to interrupt Clionel's attack animation, finally letting him inside once he's done with his backswing animation.

Keep spamming Manic Lion Cats and [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cats]]. At this point Cleanerbot Cat will reach the frontlines, giving Bahamut some protection while you build up a giant wall of apex predators. With good enough timing, your units will either destroy the base, or kill Clionel, both winning you the game.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Works great as a third meatshield along with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Erasers]]. Can tank hits from Clionel, which makes him useful as erasers will die. Just make sure he doesn't get cursed!
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Delivery Cat]]: He can act as secondary source of DPS, as his fast speed and massive damage against [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] makes him an effective rusher. Protect him from the peons and support units, as he has very low health.
*[[A Gift of Cats (Rare Cat)|Cat's Gift]]: A useful [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|
anti-Angel]] rusher. Can be good support if you get a lucky freeze against Clionel.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]: Required if you're going for the Iron Wall or Slow Beam cheese, as it is useful for summoning Clionel and killing peons for A. Bahamut to get into Clionel's blind spot.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]]: The wall itself has proven its usefulness once more. A necessary unit if you're going to try and cheese the level along with Maglev. It can hold back the peons while your attackers smack away at Clionel.
*[[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|Ultimate Mecha-Bun]]: Even though Ultimate Mecha-Bun is a rather underwhelming unit, it is quite useful as a secondary rusher alongside A. Bahamut. With its Strong Against [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] ability, it can tank hits from the Relic Doges and kill them with ease.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Whether you're going for the page's strategy or [https://youtu.be/UK4dA85bEs0? Nurse Wuffa's strategy], Awakened Bahamut is an extremely helpful unit in taking Clionel out. When combined with Mecha-Bun, he can do all the damage, while Mecha-Bun can tank the hits. Be careful though, as one hit from Clionel and Bahamut is gone.
*[[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]]: Perfect for stalling the Relic Doges at the start.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]]: Really good to tank hits from Clionel and works as a meatshield against small groups of the peons.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: Really good against the peons and overpowered once stacked. Lets you get hits easier on the Clionel and lets Bahamut get in once you knock Clionel back. Slow speed can be a hinderance, though, especially with getting her into Clionel's blind spot.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Their high damage per hit can deal with all of the peons and do good damage to the boss herself. With [[Talents]], they can provide more money through Double Bounty and get into Clionel's blind spot without getting hit through the Move Speed Up Talent.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: Effectively a second Awakened Bahamut, see above.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: He can sneak into Clionel's blind spot and absolutely annihilate her, and is also extremely good against the Heavenly Hippoes.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: Can stunlock Clionel at the base with his knockback, and deals good DPS in general.
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]]: Anti-Angel rusher that can easily get into Clionel's blind spot and shred her HP pool whilst dealing with the peons.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: Huge health and damage with [[Wave Attack]]s help this tank walk right into the blind spot while wiping the floor with peons on the way. Fast cooldown means there will always be at least one on the field.
*[[Issun_Boshi_(Uber_Rare_Cat)|Issun Boshi]]: An anti-angel version of Bahamut who has usability both in first form as a disposable rusher and in true form as a secondary Bahamut with a fairly low cooldown.

